+## 10. Data Flow & Pipelines
+
+### 10.1 Document Upload Pipeline
+
+```
+User uploads files via POST /upload/
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 1. upload_files() ΓåÆ Save raw files to data/{user_id}/threads/{thread_id}/uploads/
+Γöé      Each file gets a timestamp-suffixed name: {name}_{timestamp}.{ext}
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 2. process_files() ΓåÆ Parse each file via extract_document()
+Γöé      Batch processing (10 concurrent files)
+Γöé      Saves parsed JSON to data/.../parsed/{name}.json
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 3. save_documents_to_store() ΓåÆ Index in ChromaDB
+Γöé      Chunks documents (512 chars, 100 overlap, sentence-boundary aware)
+Γöé      Creates embeddings via nomic-embed-text-v1.5
+Γöé      Also builds BM25 index (pickled to disk)
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 4. SQLiteManager.load_spreadsheet() ΓåÆ Load spreadsheets into SQLite
+Γöé      Only for .xlsx, .xls, .csv files
+Γöé      Smart header detection + metadata enrichment
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 5. [Background] summarize_documents()
+Γöé      Per-document summaries (chunked for large docs)
+Γöé      Global cross-document summary
+Γöé      Saves to parsed JSON + global_summary.json
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 6. [Background] create_mind_map_global() (if SWITCHES["MIND_MAP"])
+Γöé      Two-phase: node generation + RAG-based description enrichment
+Γöé      Saves to data/.../mind_maps/
+Γöé
+ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ 7. [Background] create_stop_words() (for word cloud)
+       LLM-powered domain-aware stop word extraction
+```
+
+### 10.2 Query Pipeline
+
+```
+User sends question via POST /query/
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 1. Load thread data + user instructions from MongoDB
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 2. Reload spreadsheet data into SQLiteManager (if needed)
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 3. Decomposition (if SWITCHES["DECOMPOSITION"])
+Γöé      LLM resolves context + splits into sub-queries
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 4. For each (sub-)query, run Agent graph:
+Γöé      Γöé
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ RETRIEVER
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Hybrid retrieval: ChromaDB (dense) + BM25 (sparse)
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) merging
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Cross-encoder re-ranking (ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2)
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ MMR diversity selection
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Adaptive scaling (min 10 chunks/doc, max 50 total)
+Γöé      Γöé   ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ Token-budget enforcement (80% of CONTEXT_LIMIT; drop lowest-ranked chunks)
+Γöé      Γöé
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ GENERATE
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Build prompt (question + chunks + history + summary + instructions + schema)
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Detect answer style (brief/compare/analyst/detailed)
+Γöé      Γöé   Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Call invoke_llm() with mode-specific schema
+Γöé      Γöé   ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ Parse structured output (answer, action, chunks_used, suggestions)
+Γöé      Γöé
+Γöé      ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ ROUTER ΓåÆ based on action:
+Γöé          Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ ANSWER ΓåÆ END (return answer)
+Γöé          Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ WEB_SEARCH ΓåÆ Tavily search ΓåÆ back to GENERATE
+Γöé          Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ SQL_QUERY ΓåÆ Execute SQL ΓåÆ back to GENERATE
+Γöé          Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ DOCUMENT_SUMMARIZER ΓåÆ Fetch summary ΓåÆ END or GENERATE
+Γöé          Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ GLOBAL_SUMMARIZER ΓåÆ Fetch global summary ΓåÆ END or GENERATE
+Γöé          ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ FAILURE ΓåÆ SELF_KNOWLEDGE ΓåÆ END
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 5. Combination (if decomposed)
+Γöé      Merge sub-answers into coherent response
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 6. Post-process
+Γöé      Compute confidence, deduplicate suggestions
+Γöé
+ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ 7. Persist to MongoDB + return response
+```
+
+### 10.2.1 Exhaustive Analysis Pipeline (mode = "exhaustive")
+
+When the user selects "Deep Analysis" mode, the query bypasses the default RAG agent entirely
+and runs a map/reduce pipeline over ALL documents in the thread:
+
+```
+User sends question via POST /query/ with mode="exhaustive"
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 1. Load ALL parsed documents from data/.../parsed/*.json
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 2. Batch documents by BATCH_DOCUMENT_LIMIT (default 5)
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 3. MAP phase ΓÇö sequential per batch:
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Concatenate all page text from batch documents
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ chunk_page_text() ΓåÆ sentence-boundary chunks (512 chars, 100 overlap)
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ rerank_chunks() ΓåÆ cross-encoder re-ranking (top MAX_TOTAL_CHUNKS per batch)
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Token-budget enforcement (80% of CONTEXT_LIMIT; drop lowest-ranked chunks)
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Build map prompt (query + reranked context + batch_id)
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ invoke_llm() ΓåÆ ExhaustiveMapOutput (key_findings, evidence, contradictions, partial_answer)
+Γöé      ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ Emit exhaustive_progress Socket.IO event (batch N/total)
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 4. REDUCE phase ΓÇö single or recursive:
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ If only 1 batch: skip reduce, promote map output directly
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ Serialize all batch outputs ΓåÆ count tokens
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ If under 80% of CONTEXT_LIMIT: single reduce call
+Γöé      Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ If over budget: recursive grouping (sub-groups of 4) ΓåÆ intermediate reduces ΓåÆ repeat
+Γöé      ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ invoke_llm() ΓåÆ ExhaustiveReduceOutput (final_answer, consensus_points, contradictions, confidence)
+Γöé
+Γö£ΓöÇΓöÇ 5. Persist user + agent messages to MongoDB
+Γöé
+ΓööΓöÇΓöÇ 6. Return response with exhaustive=True + exhaustive_meta
 ```
 
-### Testing (uses Makefile.test)
+**Socket.IO progress events:** The backend emits `exhaustive_progress` events to the Socket.IO session
+identified by `sid` (passed in the request body). The frontend creates a short-lived socket connection
+before sending the query, listens for progress updates, and disconnects afterwards.
+
